//! Parameter names per function, so a named argument lands in the
//! right slot.
//!
//! Generated by `tools/paramnames.py` from the Creation Kit's own
//! `Scripts.zip`. Do not edit by hand.
//!
//! `Game.DisablePlayerControls(abMovement = false, abMenu = false,
//! abActivate = false, abFighting = true)` writes **all nine** parameters:
//! the four named values at their declared slots and the other five at
//! their defaults. Placing them positionally puts `false` where
//! `abMovement` and `abFighting` belong, which is a call that runs with
//! the wrong booleans rather than one that differs in numbering.
//!
//! A name is kept only when every declaration that reaches it agrees, on
//! the same rule the type and default tables use: a name declared two
//! different ways cannot settle a position.

